DeschutesCounty
Copyright Jared Folkins 2011-2026

Description:

  This is a web scraping program written to mine the
  Deschutes County website public foreclosure records.
  The collected data is used to track how many foreclosures
  are coming to market and to better understand buying
  opportunities.

2026 Note:

  This README was refreshed in 2026 for clarity. Command-line
  behavior remains the same, and examples below continue to work.

Options:

  --page=PAGE                  Crawl a specific page's tree. PAGE takes precedence over SKIP. An error occurs if YEAR is also set.
  --skip=SKIP                  Skip forward a certain number of pages on the search results page.
  --year=YEAR                  Crawl documents by year.
  --limit=LIMIT                Limit the total number of search result pages to crawl (primarily used to refresh the dataset without crawling the full archive).
  --trace=TRACE                Enable Memprof to profile code.

Examples:

  $ ruby worker_bot.rb -h

Descriptions:

--page: go to the page with instrument_id 920850

  $ ruby worker_bot.rb --page 920850

--skip: skip the first 15 pages of search results

  $ ruby worker_bot.rb --skip 15

--year: only crawl records for 2006

  $ ruby worker_bot.rb --year 2006

--limit: only crawl N search result pages

  $ ruby worker_bot.rb --limit 10

--trace: enable memprof

  $ ruby worker_bot.rb --trace true

Mix and Match: search only year 2001 and skip 5 pages

  $ ruby worker_bot.rb --year 2001 --skip 5
